#%PAM-1.0
# Solium's lock screen. Solium's helper, solium-auth, checks the password a
# locked session's user types against this service, and nothing else: it
# authenticates, then asks whether the account may still come in (expired,
# locked, outside its hours), so the auth and account stacks are used, and
# both must be here: an empty account stack refuses everyone. They are the
# ones the console login uses, so the lock accepts exactly what logging in
# accepts.
#
# Installed as /etc/pam.d/solium: by the Fedora package, by
# `dev/install.sh --prefix /usr`, or, for an install into your home, by the
# sudo line dev/install.sh prints. `solium --check` says whether it is there.
auth       include      login
account    include      login
